SUMMARY:Legacy Trust Information Session
DESCRIPTION:Legacy Trust Information Session\nSeptember 2\, 2026\n2:30-3:30 p.m.\nJoin us for a Special Legacy Trust Information Session on September 2 \nGrow your legacy at The North Carolina Arboretum\, join the Legacy Trust–the Arboretum’s society for planned giving. By including The North Carolina Arboretum Society in your estate plan\, you ensure that our Southern Appalachian mountain landscapes\, conservation efforts and education programs endure for future generations. \nLegacy Trust Information Session\nWed\, Sept. 2 from 2:30 – 3:30 p.m.\nThe North Carolina Arboretum – Education Center Library\nSpace is limited. RSVP by August 27 to development@ncarboretum.org \nYou’re invited to an informative and thoughtful session focused on tax-wise legacy planning\, where you’ll gain insight on developing a plan that benefits your loved ones and the community for years to come. \nWe are excited to welcome Kinna Clark\, Senior Director of Development and Gift Planning Services of The University of North Carolina System Office\, who will share practical strategies to maximize legacy giving. \nWhether you are just beginning to think about your will and bequests\, or already have a plan in place\, you’ll walk away with useful\, actionable information. Space is limited. For more information and to RSVP contact development@ncarboretum.org or visit https://ncarboretum.org/donate/planned-giving/.
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/legacy-trust-information-session/
LOCATION:Education Center Library
