SUMMARY:Franklinia Tree Paper Flower Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Franklinia Tree Paper Flower Workshop\nwith Cynthia Woodsong \nFriday\, September 4  |  11am – 4pm \nRegister Here!\n  \nJoin naturalist Cynthia Woodsong in this informative and hands-on workshop learning how to create botanically accurate paper flowers and leaves of the unique Franklinia alatamaha\, the beautiful and enigmatic shrub or small tree described by William Bartram in the late 18th century. This workshop starts by joining the Lunch & Learn program led by Jim Costa\, which includes a talk and guided observation of the impressive specimen at the Arboretum.  Following the talk\, workshop participants will use their new knowledge to help guide them in creating paper flowers and leaves on an actual Franklinia branch under Cynthia’s direction. All materials are provided. \nCynthia Woodsong is a North Carolina Master Naturalist with a certificate in Botanical Art and Illustration from the North Carolina Botanical Garden\, UNC Chapel Hill. Her work focuses primarily on making realistic paper replicas of flowering plants native to the southeastern United States and conducting workshops to teach the craft to others. These paper plants are then placed in clay pots or other containers. Cynthia also incorporates paper botanicals in her “3-D botanical plates\,” rendered in watercolor or colored pencil. Her work can be seen at woodsongbotanicals.org\, and at the North Carolina Botanical Garden in Chapel Hill\, NC. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/franklinia-tree-paper-flower-workshop/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
