SUMMARY:Blooms in a Hoop: Beginner Embroidery Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Blooms in a Hoop: Beginner Embroidery Workshop\nwith JeanAnne Taylor \nThursday\, September 10  |  12 – 4pm \nRegister Here!\n  \nStudents will learn basic techniques of hand embroidery\, as well as information on needle sizes\, types of floss\, and appropriate fabric. I will demonstrate how to do the embroidery stitches\, then work one on one if necessary for students to understand. I will provide a supply kit for the students. They will have a finished (or mostly finished) project to take home. \nJeanAnn Taylor loves to be creative with words\, watercolors\, hooks\, yarn\, dancing\, gardening\, fabric\, and thread. As an award-winning embroidery artist\, she combines her love of nature with original embroidery designs. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
